\b Meeting: Supervisor Meeting — 2025-10-10\b0\par
Attendees: Liu Chen; Prof. Henry C. B. Chan\par
\par
\b Agenda\b0\par
\bullet\tab Review classic strategy results vs Buy&Hold\par
\bullet\tab Discuss ML baseline design (labels, features, walk-forward)\par
\par
\b Progress Since Last Meeting\b0\par
\bullet\tab Implemented and ran classic strategies; exported equity curves and summary tables.\par
\bullet\tab Observed several strategies show decent Sharpe but low coverage/exposure.\par
\par
\b Discussion / Supervisor Feedback\b0\par
\bullet\tab Supervisor noted that low coverage may look good on Sharpe but will lag Buy&Hold in trending markets.\par
\bullet\tab Discussed 3-class labeling (Up/Neutral/Down) to avoid forcing trades during small moves.\par
\par
\b Decisions\b0\par
\bullet\tab Adopt volatility-adaptive dynamic threshold labeling using rolling volatility (shifted to avoid leakage).\par
\bullet\tab Use a cost-aware backtest with confidence threshold and minimum holding period.\par
\par
\b Action Items (Next Steps)\b0\par
\bullet\tab Implement LSTM classification baseline and standardize outputs (metrics, preds, backtest stats).\par
\bullet\tab Add a clear “probabilities → trades” explanation section to the report.\par
